{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793652149,"nonce":"zqG5tTftqDzzOcDhAir0yNvG8q8=","title":"Restore Cloud Sync write-back credentials and merge bases after compute recovery","message":"Parent: cd54ac37bbbdfea0fa1fcd39288738a7c0b48475ed9ecea3e6cc98ad20c109ed.\n\nDuring gateway egress work, the runner recovery path still calls launch_session(record, None), as does restarting a stopped session inside a live guest. A newly authorized Open may carry a fresh publish capability, but these paths do not pass it through. The replacement session therefore has no RAYDE_SYNC_* environment and loses Cloud Sync save-back availability.\n\nSimply forwarding the latest capability is insufficient: native/session Writeback keeps its three-way merge Base only in memory. After publish/merge it can differ from the original restored generation, and unsaved local files on persistent disks are not a trustworthy replacement for that common base. Re-capturing the current tree as though it were the newest remote generation could overwrite newer remote edits.\n\nPersist the acknowledged base generation/manifest and bounded merge text privately under the session state directory, with atomic durable ordering relative to publication and merge. Recover it from the same verified persistent disks. Reauthorize and renew the workspace-scoped publish capability on restart/recovery without writing the capability into durable records or returning it to browsers/child programs. Refuse write-back when lineage is missing rather than synthesizing a base from edited files. Refresh the browser's save-back status after recovery. Handle expiry while a guest remains alive too.\n\nCover saved local changes, unsaved CRDT edits, newer remote generations, token expiry, missing/corrupt base data, killed session, killed VM and runner restart. Verify ordinary repository guests never acquire a capability and foreign workspace credentials remain rejected. This is separate from continuous live Yrs synchronization and from gateway-host egress (9de223d).","files":null}]}